      Most garage door failures don’t happen suddenly. They build over time from wear,
      friction, and unnoticed part fatigue. Routine inspection and adjustment prevents
      broken springs, snapped cables, door-off-track situations, and premature opener failure.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>High-tension springs under extreme pressure</li>
      <li>Cables carrying the full weight of the door</li>
      <li>Rollers, hinges, and bearings that wear with every cycle</li>
