<div class="reveal-on-scroll">
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-question">
      <span>How often should I have my garage door professionally serviced?</span>
      <span class="faq-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-answer">
      <p>Most residential garage doors should be professionally serviced at least once per year. If you use your door heavily (multiple times per day), have an older system (15+ years), or notice any unusual sounds or behavior, twice-per-year maintenance is recommended. Annual maintenance catches wear before it leads to expensive breakdowns.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
 
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-question">
      <span>What does garage door maintenance include?</span>
      <span class="faq-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-answer">
      <p>Our maintenance service includes a full mechanical inspection of springs, cables, rollers, hinges, and tracks; professional lubrication of all moving parts; door balance testing and adjustment; safety system testing (photo eyes and auto-reverse); opener force and travel checks; and a written condition report identifying any components that need attention. The goal is to catch small issues before they become failures.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
 
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-question">
      <span>Can I do garage door maintenance myself?</span>
      <span class="faq-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-answer">
      <p>You can handle basic maintenance like cleaning tracks, checking for obstructions, and visual inspections. However, spring tension testing, cable inspection, door balancing, and safety system calibration require professional tools and expertise. Springs are under extreme tension and can cause serious injury if handled improperly. We recommend DIY for basic cleaning and visual checks, but professional service annually for thorough inspection and adjustment. Check out our <a href="/blog/diy-garage-door-maintenance-tips" style="color: #c57b30;">DIY maintenance guide</a> for what you can safely do yourself.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
 
  <div class="faq-item">
    <div class="faq-question">
      <span>What are signs my garage door needs maintenance?</span>
      <span class="faq-arrow">&#9654;</span>
    </div>
